  "publicDocumentation": [
    {
      "url": "https://www.jetbrains.com/help/go/2026.1/viewing-structure-and-hierarchy-of-the-source-code.html",
      "versionHeader": "GoLand 2026.1 Help",
      "publishedDate": "2026-06-17",
      "paraphrase": "Type navigation relates concrete types and interfaces; call navigation has incoming and outgoing views for functions/methods. The Hierarchy window supports retaining results, refreshing, expanding and opening source. Documented call options include selected search scopes and interface-aware calls. These are public described capabilities, not observed commercial runtime outcomes."
    },
    {
      "url": "https://www.jetbrains.com/help/go/2026.1/viewing-structure-of-a-source-file.html",
      "versionHeader": "GoLand 2026.1 Help",
      "publishedDate": "2025-09-12",
      "paraphrase": "Both a popup and a persistent tool window expose source elements and support typing-based navigation. Go-specific controls include other files in the package, alphabetical/export ordering, and private-element visibility. The page names interfaces, fields, functions, methods, types, variables and constants."
    },
    {
      "url": "https://www.jetbrains.com/help/go/2026.1/structure-tool-window-file-structure-popup.html",
      "versionHeader": "GoLand 2026.1 Help",
      "publishedDate": "2025-11-06",
      "paraphrase": "The Structure pane follows the active editor or selected project file. Its common controls include expansion/collapse, speed search, one-click source navigation and selection following the caret. Language-specific options coexist with general tool-window controls."
    }
  ],
  "inference": [
    "The Go plugin delegates to standard IntelliJ hierarchy and structure extension points; independent implementations should integrate these native hosts rather than imitate a hierarchy in an unrelated custom list.",
    "Go type hierarchy must use Go interface satisfaction semantics, including value/pointer receiver differences, rather than Java inheritance assumptions.",
    "The standard global MethodHierarchy action does not establish a dedicated working Go method-hierarchy provider.",
    "The shipped macOS literal map gives Ctrl+H for TypeHierarchy, Ctrl+Alt+H for CallHierarchy, and Cmd+7 for Structure. FileStructurePopup was observed only in the default map at Ctrl+F12; effective macOS mapping is not established by this bounded inventory."
  ],
  "unknown": [
    "No reference application runtime was exercised. Actual available targets, dynamic update states, laziness, expansion, selection, titles, progress, cancellation, disposal and persistence are unverified.",
    "Exact generic/constraint/alias handling, pointer/value presentation and package/library reachability of commercial type hierarchy are unverified.",
    "Interface-call expansion, recursion/cycle rendering, call-site multiplicity and the exact effects of hierarchy scopes require runtime evidence.",
    "Commercial dirty-document/version behavior, UTF-16 locations, undo/redo refresh, and handling of removed symbols remain unverified.",
    "The public private-member example ambiguously suggests an exported item is excluded; do not infer private-only filtering without runtime verification.",
    "Effective user keymap and platform shortcut patches were not read from user configuration. A literal bundled mapping does not prove the active binding.",
    "PyCharm is retained in the existing installed-ides inventory as platform comparison only; no new PyCharm artifact or Python behavior claim was investigated."
